statementMd:
You are given $*N*$ qubits ($1 ≤ *N* ≤ 8$) in zero state ![image](https://espresso.codeforces.com/8bb67080da7081bfb802ca6ecc5abc4f4c5ca190.png). You are also given two bitstrings $*bits*0$ and $*bits*1$ which describe two different basis states on $*N*$ qubits ![image](https://espresso.codeforces.com/07ea1d435b195752acd41643cb12df28e6913e88.png) and ![image](https://espresso.codeforces.com/0648292c6f022bae2c3c2bc8fb76f00714a57bd9.png).

Your task is to generate a state which is an equal superposition of the given basis states:

![image](https://espresso.codeforces.com/8bca7f237006a9be77ba507b8c1faac217c6a5b3.png)

You have to implement an operation which takes the following inputs:

- an array of qubits $*qs*$,
- two arrays of Boolean values $*bits*0$ and $*bits*1$ representing the basis states ![image](https://espresso.codeforces.com/07ea1d435b195752acd41643cb12df28e6913e88.png) and ![image](https://espresso.codeforces.com/0648292c6f022bae2c3c2bc8fb76f00714a57bd9.png). These arrays will have the same length as the array of qubits. $*bits*0$ and $*bits*1$ will differ in at least one position.

The operation doesn't have an output; its "output" is the state in which it leaves the qubits.

Your code should have the following signature:

```
namespace Solution {
    open Microsoft.Quantum.Primitive;
    open Microsoft.Quantum.Canon;

    operation Solve (qs : Qubit[], bits0 : Bool[], bits1 : Bool[]) : ()
    {
        body
        {
            // your code here
        }
    }
}
```

